    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=temasek#/JobDescription/17679049/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b086-1ffe18ca540b": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/12/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 29 Dec 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineering What you will be working on Deliver lessons to full-time diploma students and part-time adult learners, and undertake all related academic responsibilities. Design, develop, and deliver curriculum, courseware, and e-learning modules for assigned full-time and part-time programmes. Supervise and assess student projects and internships in collaboration with industry partners. Apply relevant IT tools and multimedia platforms to enhance teaching effectiveness and student engagement. Coach and mentor students in academic development, competitions, career guidance, and personal growth. Undertake academic administration and committee work, and support outreach activities, community projects, and study trips (local and overseas). Plan, lead, and contribute to projects with industry partners, including internships and capability development initiatives. What we are looking for Qualification in Facilities Management, Mechanical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Building Sciences, or a related Built Environment discipline. At least 3 years of relevant experience in the facilities management sector or a sustainability consultancy environment. Hands-on experience in the adoption or implementation of Smart Facilities Management, BIM for FM, Digital Twin, Building IoT, and data analytics for productivity, operational efficiency, and environmental sustainability. Good knowledge of the operation and maintenance of key building systems, particularly Fire Safety Systems, Building Management Systems (BMS), Air-Conditioning and Mechanical Ventilation (ACMV) systems, and security and surveillance systems in large industrial or commercial buildings (e.g. hospitals, data centres, or other critical facilities). Relevant certifications will be an advantage, such as Fire Safety Manager (with at least 2 years’ appointment in a commercial building), Autodesk Revit Certified Professional/Associate, BIM Modelling/Management certification, Green Mark Accredited Professional (GMAP), or IT/programming certifications. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to engage and teach youth effectively. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Lecturer (Information Technology) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Sustainability Finance) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 9999 Lecturer (Architectural Technology & Building Services) / School of En Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Aviation Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Nov 2026 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Veterinary Technology) Temasek Polytechnic Closing in 6  day(s) Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Language and Communication Lecturer (Polytechnic Foundation Programme) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 22 Oct 2026 Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineerin Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=temasek#/JobDescription/17721856/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-ad8c-f09dfd20540b": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic 04-08 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 16 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This role is responsible for developing and delivering high-quality teaching in Human Resource Management with a strong emphasis on HR technology, analytics, process workflow automation and digitally enabled people practices. The role will design and review curriculum for both Pre-Employment Training (PET) and Continuing Education and Training (CET), support applied learning through industry projects, and contribute to student development, school initiatives and partnerships with industry. What you will be working on Design, develop and deliver modules in human resource management, with particular strength in areas such as HR analytics, HR technology and HR process automation, AI in HR, workforce planning, learning and talent development, performance management, and change management. Create and review teaching, learning and assessment materials for PET and CET learners to ensure curriculum relevance, rigour and employability outcomes. Keep abreast of developments in HR technology, people analytics and digital workforce transformation, and translate these into updated curriculum and learning activities. Facilitate active, practice-oriented learning through projects, case studies, simulations and authentic assessment. Collaborate with industry partners to provide consultancy, live projects, internships and other applied learning opportunities in HR transformation and people practices. Supervise student projects, internships, competitions and overseas or community-based learning activities where relevant. Support SkillsFuture, CET, work-study and other institution-level initiatives related to lifelong learning and workforce upskilling. Contribute to school, polytechnic and cross-institution committees, quality assurance processes and strategic initiatives. What we are looking for Relevant qualifications in Human Resource Management, Psychology, Business, Organisational Development, People Analytics, Information Systems / Digital Business (with HR relevance), or a related discipline. A minimum of 4 to 8 years of relevant industry experience across domains such as People Operations (HR Shared Services), People Analytics, People and Culture, HR Digital Transformation, Human Capital Management Systems, and Talent Management. Candidates with prior teaching experience, industry certifications, consultancy experience, or experience implementing HR technologies and analytics tools will have an advantage. Domain required Demonstrated ability to teach or work in at least two of the following areas: HR analytics, HR technology and automation, AI in HR, total rewards, learning and talent development, performance management, workforce planning, change management, or work behaviour. Familiarity with IHRP-related competency areas, CET programme development, and interdisciplinary teaching across business and technology subjects is desirable. Strong communication, facilitation and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to mentor students and collaborate effectively with colleagues and industry partners. A passion for education and student development, with the ability to support both academic and applied learning outcomes. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineer Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer (Information Technology) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Sustainability Finance) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 9999 Lecturer (Architectural Technology & Building Services) / School of En Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Aviation Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Nov 2026 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Veterinary Technology) Temasek Polytechnic Closing in 6  day(s) Language and Communication Lecturer (Polytechnic Foundation Programme) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 22 Oct 2026 Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineerin Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 16 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
