      "title": "Lecturer (Built Environment Technology) / School of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/12/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Lecturer (Built Environment Technology) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 30 Dec 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Lecturer (Built Environment Technology) / School of Engineering What you will be working on Design and deliver industry-relevant curriculum for full-time and continuing education programmes across architectural technology, building services, sustainability and digital delivery. Develop authentic learning experiences through case studies, projects, laboratory activities, simulations and industry-based assessments. Mentor and guide students in their learning, internships, projects, competitions and career development. Supervise student projects and work-based learning, fostering professional ethics, safety awareness and critical thinking. Engage industry, professional and public-sector stakeholders to support curriculum enhancement, applied projects and workplace learning opportunities. Contribute to curriculum review and quality improvement by incorporating industry developments, regulatory changes and learner feedback. Apply emerging technologies and digital practices such as BIM, Integrated Digital Delivery, AI-enabled workflows and smart-building technologies in teaching and project work. Maintain professional currency in Built Environment practices, technologies and sustainability trends, and translate these into teaching and programme development. Support school initiatives including outreach, student recruitment, industry engagement, continuing education and multidisciplinary projects. What we are looking for · A relevant qualification in architecture, architectural technology, building services engineering, sustainability, construction management or a related Built Environment discipline. · At least three years of relevant industry experience in areas such as consultancy, project delivery, facilities management, sustainability, digital construction or related Built Environment practice. · Experience in one or more of the following areas: o   architectural technology and multidisciplinary coordination; o   building services design and integration; o   sustainability and building-performance analysis; o   BIM, VDC, Integrated Digital Delivery or Common Data Environment workflows; o   digital construction, smart buildings or data-driven solutions. · Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to explain technical concepts effectively to diverse learners. · Ability to mentor, coach and motivate students in their academic and professional development. · Strong collaboration and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to work across disciplines and industry sectors. · An adaptable and improvement-oriented mindset, with interest in emerging technologies and innovative teaching practices. · Commitment to continuous learning and professional development. · Ability to work independently while contributing effectively within a collaborative academic environment. · Professional registration, accreditation or industry certifications will be an advantage. · Prior experience in training, coaching, workplace mentoring or knowledge-sharing is advantageous. Formal teaching experience is not required. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineer Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer (Information Technology) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Sustainability Finance) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 9999 Lecturer (Architectural Technology & Building Services) / School of En Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Aviation Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Nov 2026 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Veterinary Technology) Temasek Polytechnic Closing in 6  day(s) Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineerin Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Built Environment Technology) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 APPLY NOW"
