      "title": "Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/12/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 30 Dec 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineering What you will be working on Design, develop, and test electronic hardware and embedded systems for healthcare engineering applications, including analogue and digital circuit design, PCB design, firmware development, and system integration. Develop, troubleshoot, and validate prototypes and instrumentation systems through laboratory testing, system verification, and performance characterisation. Analyse and resolve complex technical challenges independently, applying sound engineering principles, professional judgement, and practical experience. Lead and deliver funded R&D, industry collaboration, and consultancy projects, including technical planning, stakeholder engagement, vendor management, milestone tracking, and project execution. Prepare and maintain technical documentation, including schematics, PCB layouts, design files, bills of materials, test plans, technical reports, and user documentation. Collaborate with multidisciplinary teams and external stakeholders, including industry, healthcare, clinical, research, and government partners, to develop and translate innovative technologies into practical applications. Provide technical leadership and mentorship to engineers, technical officers, students, and project teams, while promoting engineering excellence, quality standards, and laboratory safety. Identify, evaluate, and develop innovative technologies and solutions with potential for commercialisation, intellectual property creation, and industry impact. Serve as a subject matter expert in electronics, embedded systems, and instrumentation, providing technical guidance and strategic direction across projects and functional teams. Lead the architecture, development, and integration of complex systems, taking ownership of technical decisions, risk management, and project outcomes. Drive technology innovation, intellectual property generation, and translational research activities, supporting technology transfer, licensing, industry adoption, and capability development initiatives. What we are looking for Relevant qualification in Electrical/Electronic Engineering or a related discipline. Relevant industry experience in circuit design, PCB design and fabrication, and embedded systems programming is essential. Experience in firmware development, hardware-software integration, and system integration will be advantageous. At least 5 years of relevant industry or R&D experience, with demonstrated hands-on expertise in electronics development and a proven track record of leading and delivering industry or research projects. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently as well as collaboratively in multidisciplinary teams. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Experience in grant proposal writing and the management of funded R&D projects will be an advantage. Experience in healthcare engineering, medical devices, sensors, instrumentation, or other applied technology development domains will be an added advantage. Demonstrated ability to translate research outcomes into practical applications, prototypes, or commercialisable solutions is desirable. A passion for innovation, applied research, and industry collaboration, with a strong commitment to continuous learning and professional development. About Temasek Polytechnic Established in 1990, Temasek Polytechnic (TP) is a leading institution of high learning nestled by the idyllic shores of Bedok Reservoir in Tampines.  TP takes pride in equipping our students with lifelong skills and digital knowledge for a future of dynamic change.\n\nTP’s caring and vibrant culture is firmly rooted in our core values which drive a spirit of innovation, with a focus on industry, globalization and sustainability.  “TP Cares” is our clarion call to ensure that our diverse community of learners has the opportunity to achieve their personal best, so that they can contribute meaningfully to the global community.\n\nLearner. Creator. Leader\nWe envision the TP graduate as a values-led leader with vision, character and heart, excelling in the academic domain and beyond, and rising to the challenge of creating tomorrow. You might also be interested in Lecturer (Integrated & Smart Facility Management) / School of Engineer Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer (Information Technology) / School of Informatics & IT Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Dec 2026 Lecturer/Senior Lecturer (Sustainability Finance) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 9999 Lecturer (Architectural Technology & Building Services) / School of En Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Oct 2026 Lecturer (Aviation Management) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 29 Nov 2026 Lecturer / Senior Lecturer (Veterinary Technology) Temasek Polytechnic Closing in 6  day(s) Senior Lecturer/Lecturer (HR Tech, Analytics, AI in HR) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 16 Oct 2026 Language and Communication Lecturer (Polytechnic Foundation Programme) Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 22 Oct 2026 Senior/Engineer (Healthcare Engineering Center) / School of Engineering Temasek Polytechnic Closing on 30 Dec 2026 APPLY NOW"
